  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nWe propose a refined approach that combines convex relaxation with gradient-based optimization, focusing on directly minimizing the maximum overlap. The key innovations are:\n\na) Formulate the problem with an overlapping constraints structure that allows gradient computation without circularity issues.\nb) Use Lagrangian relaxation to handle the non-convex maximum in the objective.\nc) Apply a structured perturbation scheme that respects the periodicity and overlap structure while maintaining feasibility.\nd) Incorporate a repair mechanism that exactly satisfies both the sum and pointwise constraints.\n\nThis approach addresses the limitations of simulated annealing by providing a more directed search while preserving feasibility at every step.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\nWe represent h as a vector in R^{n_points} with:\n- 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n- sum(h) = n_points / 2\n\nThe objective is:\nC\u2085 = max_{k=-(n_points-1)}^{n_points-1} (convolve(h, 1-h)[n_points + k] * dx)\n\nWe introduce a Lagrange multiplier \u03bb for the maximum constraint and use a surrogate loss:\nL(h, \u03bb) = sum_{k} \u03bb_k (convolve(h, 1-h)[k] * dx - C\u2085)\n\nwith \u03bb_k \u2265 0 and sum(\u03bb_k) = 1.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\na) Initialize:\n   - Set n_points = 100, dx = 2/n_points\n   - Use initial_h_values if available, interpolating to match n_points\n   - Clip and repair to ensure feasibility\n\nb) Main optimization loop:\n   - Compute current overlap correlations\n   - Identify the k with maximum overlap\n   - Formulate gradient descent step on h to reduce this overlap\n   - Apply perturbation: h += -learning_rate * grad\n   - Repair h to maintain constraints\n   - Track best solution\n\nc) Repair mechanism:\n   1. Clip h to [0,1]\n   2. Compute scaling factor s = (n_points/2) / sum(h)\n   3. Set h = h * s\n\nd) Gradient computation:\n   For each h[i], compute the sensitivity of the maximum overlap to changes in h[i]\n\ne) Termination:\n   - Stop after budget_s seconds\n   - Record best solution encountered\n\n4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Learning rate: Start at 1e-4, reduce by factor of 0.99 every 100 steps\n- Initial random perturbations: Magnitude 0.05\n- Maximum iterations: 10,000\n- Use two repair passes to ensure both constraints are met\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Each iteration takes ~1ms, allowing ~1e6 iterations in budget\n- Gradient computation is O(n_points^2)\n- Robust to numerical errors via repair mechanism\n- Safe fallback to initial_h_values if needed\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Verify sum(h) == n_points/2 within 1e-8\n- Ensure all h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\n- Recompute C\u2085 via evaluate_h to confirm\n- Check for NaNs/infs in h and C\u2085",
